#version 450
// The sharpening of the finished frame (docs/USER_GUIDE.md, "Sharpening"; crates/layer/src/sharpen.rs): applied at
// present to the swapchain image's raw words (copied into `Src`, written into `Dst`, copied back), after all of
// the layer's own work, on every presented frame. Both filters are off by default; with both off nothing is
// dispatched. One invocation a pixel (phases 0-2: a pixel of the half-size luma grid).
//
// Phase 0: the frame's luma at half size (the mean of each 2x2 block), for Clarity's base.
// Phase 1: the base along the rows: a Gaussian (sigma half the radius) whose taps are weighted down where their
//          luma differs from the centre's (the edge stop, against halos at strong edges).
// Phase 2: the same down the columns.
// Phase 3: per pixel, CAS (FidelityFX Contrast Adaptive Sharpening, sharpen-only path, ported below) on the
//          3x3 neighbourhood, then Clarity: the pixel's luma minus the base (read bilinearly), weighted toward the
//          midtones, added to all three channels; then the HUD regions move the result back toward the frame
//          (keep: none of it inside, soften: its strength), over a feather outside each rectangle.
//
// The words are the swapchain's: 8 bits a channel (RGBA8 or BGRA8, UNORM or SRGB alike: the encoded values are
// filtered) or 10 bits (A2B10G10R10 / A2R10G10B10, the HDR10 PQ code values), alpha kept bit for bit. A pixel
// nothing changes is written back exactly.
//
// The CAS part is a port of AMD FidelityFX CAS 1.20190610 (ffx_cas.h, CasFilter with noScaling,
// CAS_BETTER_DIAGONALS and CAS_GO_SLOWER, the green channel's weight for all three, the "UNORM with linear
// conversion approximation" input: squared on load, square root on store). Its sharpness maps to the peak weight
// as -s / lerp(8, 5, s), so the strength starts from nothing (CAS's own -1 / lerp(8, 5, s) starts at -1/8; its
// default, sharpness 0, is strength 8/11 here).
//
